{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-21T10:59:40.724Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the explicit archive timestamp requirement within scope (`src/watcher/archiver.ts`, `tests/archiver.test.ts`).\n\n**Implementation**\n- `archiveSpecFolder` now appends exactly one change-level `archived` event via the append-only `appendHarnessEvent` writer to `<archived>/.run/events/change.jsonl`, strictly after `fs.rename` and `ensureArchivedTasksTicked` succeed. Timestamp is `new Date().toISOString()` (authoritative archive time). No numbered task file receives it.\n- Failed relocation throws before emission; failed archive verification returns before `archiveSpecFolder` is called, so no `archived` event in either case.\n\n**Tests** (4 new, 13/13 pass)\n- Direct archive emits one `archived` event with ISO time inside the relocation window, `data.archivePath`, and only `change.jsonl` in the events dir.\n- Failed relocation rejects with no event.\n- Blocked change-level verify emits no `archived`, keeps the change active, and retains `verify_ran` + `regressed` diagnostics.\n- Successful `checkAndArchiveSpec` yields the archived stream ordered `verify_ran` then `archived`.\n\n**Verification**: `node --import tsx --test tests/archiver.test.ts` 13/13; `pnpm verify` exit 0.\n\n**Note**: Task 1 did not actually add the typed `archived` member to `src/harness/types.ts` as this task's details assumed, and `types.ts` is listed only as `entry` (not `scope`). To stay in scope I declared `ArchivedEventData` locally and used a single `as unknown as HarnessEvent` cast on the existing writer. Documented in `.run/results/4.md` as the remaining follow-up."}}
